=== task: mcq medium
title: How many loop steps?
prompt: `count` runs on an n-ary tree of n nodes. Over all the calls together, how many times does the line `total += count(child)` run?
* n − 1: once for every edge, because every node except the root is exactly one node's child :: Right.
- n: once for every node :: The root is nobody's child, so it's never counted by this line.
- n²: each node loops over every other node :: Each node loops only over its own children.
- It depends on how many children the widest node has :: However the children are spread out, the lists hold n − 1 nodes in total.
hint: The line runs once for each child in each list.
hint: Which node is in no children list?
right: The children lists hold every node except the root, so the loop runs n − 1 times in all: count is O(n) whatever the shape.
wrong: Every node but the root appears in exactly one parent's children list, and the line runs once per entry: n − 1 times.

